<!-- FAQ -->
<section class="section" id="faq">
  <h2>7. Automotive Aerosol Products FAQs</h2>
  <div style="margin-top: 20px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 16px;">
    <details style="border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: var(--radius-lg); padding: 16px 20px;">
      <summary style="font-weight: 700; cursor: pointer; font-family: 'Outfit', sans-serif; font-size: 1.05rem;">What are the main categories of automotive aerosol products?</summary>
      <p style="margin-top: 12px;">The main categories are mechanical and maintenance products, performance cleaners, and electrical care products. Examples are engine degreasers and penetrating oils, brake and throttle body cleaners, and dielectric contact cleaners. Aesthetic and interior products such as dashboard polish and tyre shiner form another category. Protective coatings such as underbody anti-rust sprays and zinc primers complete the range.</p>
    </details>
    <details style="border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: var(--radius-lg); padding: 16px 20px;">
      <summary style="font-weight: 700; cursor: pointer; font-family: 'Outfit', sans-serif; font-size: 1.05rem;">Which propellants are used in automotive aerosols?</summary>
      <p style="margin-top: 12px;">Propellants are either liquefied gases such as LPG and DME or compressed gases such as CO2 and nitrogen. Each affects the spray pattern and the pressure profile over the life of the can. LPG suits high-pressure delivery, while CO2 suits non-flammable or environmentally sensitive applications. Valve and actuator choices then shape how that pressure reaches the surface.</p>
    </details>
    <details style="border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: var(--radius-lg); padding: 16px 20px;">
      <summary style="font-weight: 700; cursor: pointer; font-family: 'Outfit', sans-serif; font-size: 1.05rem;">Why do automotive aerosols use 360-degree valves?</summary>
      <p style="margin-top: 12px;">A 360-degree valve lets the product be sprayed from any angle, which is crucial in tight engine bays where the can cannot stay upright. Actuator nozzles then set the pattern, from wide-angle mists for large surfaces to extension-straw streams for pinpoint accuracy.</p>
    </details>
    <details style="border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: var(--radius-lg); padding: 16px 20px;">
      <summary style="font-weight: 700; cursor: pointer; font-family: 'Outfit', sans-serif; font-size: 1.05rem;">What safety and quality controls apply to manufacturing automotive aerosols?</summary>
      <p style="margin-top: 12px;">Filling flammable propellants requires explosion-proof equipment, advanced ventilation, and specialized gassing houses that isolate the propellant. Each batch is tested for pressure stability, leakage, and spray performance, and hydrostatic testing confirms that containers withstand pressures above their working range. Batch coding provides traceability from the production line to the end user.</p>
    </details>
    <details style="border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: var(--radius-lg); padding: 16px 20px;">
      <summary style="font-weight: 700; cursor: pointer; font-family: 'Outfit', sans-serif; font-size: 1.05rem;">How do VOC rules affect automotive aerosol formulations?</summary>
      <p style="margin-top: 12px;">VOC rules restrict the volatile organic content of consumer products, and California's CARB sets these limits by product category across more than 130 categories. Automotive cleaners such as brake cleaners and engine degreasers fall within that framework. Formulators must meet the limits without sacrificing cleaning power.</p>
    </details>
    <details style="border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: var(--radius-lg); padding: 16px 20px;">
      <summary style="font-weight: 700; cursor: pointer; font-family: 'Outfit', sans-serif; font-size: 1.05rem;">Can a startup launch an automotive aerosol brand without its own filling plant?</summary>
      <p style="margin-top: 12px;">Yes. Contract filling gives a startup access to established filling lines, R&amp;D laboratories, and supply chains without the capital expenditure of a full-scale facility. The startup then focuses on branding, marketing, and distribution while the contract filler handles production.</p>
    </details>
  </div>
</section>

